  "interpretation": {
    "ratio_direction": "Preble / round-robin: values below 1 mean lower Preble latency.",
    "percentiles": "Linear interpolation over all 786 raw request observations per policy/rate; never an average of trial percentiles.",
    "cache_fraction": "Sum cached tokens / sum prompt tokens across requests.",
    "throughput": "Successful requests or output tokens / sum of complete trial durations, including arrival wait and tail drain.",
    "generation_cap": "Outputs are validated against the frozen runtime's effective cap: max(0, min(requested cap, min(context_length-1, token_capacity-1)-prompt_tokens-1, token_capacity-ceil_page(prompt_tokens)-page_size-1)). With context 32768 and page size 1, a 32722-token prompt has an effective cap of 44 despite the requested 45; a length finish must equal the effective cap."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "All MPQ trials precede the LPM phase; policies are not temporally alternated, so phase/time effects remain confounded.",
    "Only two trials per policy/rate. Pooled requests share document prefixes and trial conditions; 786 requests are not 786 independent experimental repetitions.",
    "TTFT and E2E include client semaphore queue time. Actual late-wakeup delay relative to the planned arrival is not archived.",
    "The replay permits 256 concurrent HTTP requests. Client-queue mean/p95/max show waiting before HTTP admission; a backlog above that limit delays the offered arrival trace at the client.",
    "Only the eight fixed completed generation trials are summarized. Archived operational preflight failures are excluded; runner execution revisions retain separate manifest hashes.",
    "This is Preble+MPQ versus round-robin+LPM: global routing and local scheduling change together; the global-router effect is not isolated.",
    "Output token counts and finish reasons are recorded; output text is not archived and answer quality is not evaluated.",
    "Output hash/token agreement is descriptive, not a pass/fail condition: temperature-zero outputs can vary with batch shapes and numerical effects. This is a performance validation, not a LooGLE answer-quality evaluation.",
    "This uses Qwen3-235B and the current SGLang runtime; it is not a same-model/same-hardware reproduction of the paper's performance.",
    "Backend release versions and all reported static settings are compared; full version git suffixes and frontend commits are archived separately."
  ]
